eugX-nwDueErrJvsoIIrut1I8vd6hKgyf3iydjNHgdwjUCTDq_GaCjnwAeBxv8--5xQL_sdFbQ9f2o8TO0suHs-_kLGNQ8PJ0zdqPaWel3dEUKXU8VT0BZFJrlgLuAPq7cXVE_P_RuouxpnCrit-geR0DcearOC-Jj_Skorh04X5sGe77DlISa25GvfCNisDN3iMaF6CPgzmcX6B81eM9xt7N99S5z_-SHqAY1hG_cK4EQzFc0Fdd8y6_56F0Xdq-pavtQQUywT2nH8xG6eZqdx1VcHcf0JBl6_xpn2s2n9-52Dqu14gdxUev93ixfbAKwxhijWTVK5rS66wPMsR4Wu26fPD0Wx7lSgQBZzbCMYubcenbVGYJTXDaUE1fNFUkGYKnUL23ogTBhO0UfNWZwzUPXVrqnBTmW1Ve_AHauvTnuZU5f_B8ud-cbZiu3RuA3rguxyNAL34CqGO9RAdcUiK2K-TuHnsm0ZBfpqUFyOEV90yU75tEOtP6EFZp_HseDlF3UunO38GcRijnLpebepwf8ZzI7h2EL-wrgIIZ5WTYvi3jpeJnmVQB8a-DiiCwhx5biioZhAkNpgOCiUqD-2NAzpP4BVctbq35xgOfJCVxgWlW_1-T-aPeXE6bTopaw0RkypdMo5CwiYRDYoZc334VBS_ZYu3wfsHhfu-c2BqjzFUJhU81KvsTSpHhjjNLnSEXa8s6XAWdWTcgeuQ0PPWaWFKK5Q2CDZSwyROvCULn32kuItJP9T6QXmr8Mb5Aws84w3MeFF_wbYGbRyQqOpl7PW8blomb6qINFrmNd4yGkr50wZUJPftw0vx6J4gRZN3QbJ9VhObuq1aJoJGFET3lSy89N4P4IPdRP00vR7lYr8ioTHxNhmZEk6pnWd0mrE4Og788_674nVOGZQyEh6XcmjHRI5EQ_Jk-FVCRD5O3mhaiRjb0G7ZMJWm5MRtxeBQQn4-7ukczrqP0rlD32fMS8-V2J3qH4hWdYKJJvKwYIu7AB4Yj_5cs-mjYJCp9auSepUHMlbvI9OIofLdrJ"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae4a29a6a2881918c58d23c338d060d","call_id":"call_38deb40c76f840388ca905cbbdb4c56b","name":"record_author_checks","arguments":"{\"candidate\":4,\"original_context_note\":\"Compared spec.full_target with target-selection.json/full_target and problem.md:19-48: the complete selected target, including the disclosed fixed-unit-vector perturbation interpretation, is preserved verbatim. Positive integer dimensions are represented by natural parameters with their positivity explicitly in H001, not granted through parameter refinements. H002 is joint smoothness, H003 is the original |q|=1, H004 is the pointwise unit constraint, H005 is pointwise existential normality with no scalar regularity, and H006 is support common to each closed positive-time slab. All six original conditions remain graph roots. H003 is unused; the proof needs q to be fixed, but not its unit norm. D001-D005 define exactly the componentwise temporal/spatial derivatives and their indices; their total derivative conventions grant no regularity and agree with classical derivatives wherever the direct smoothness input applies. D006 is the componentwise Laplacian. D007 preserves precisely the original sum of norm squares, Frobenius identification, Lebesgue measure and normalization, and D008 merely names its derivative. D009 is guarded by N002's actual all-positive-time integrability, proved without E in R002; R003 and R005 both have N002 as a direct input before using E. All other definitions are total notation and have no existence guard. The nine selected native source contracts M001,M002,M003,M005-M010 were compared with successful full probe signatures and their defining source passages: filter dominated convergence; the convex-set derivative norm estimate; interval FTC with endpoint differentiability and integrable derivative; continuous compact-support integrability; derivative of an inner product; symmetry of the second derivative with the minSmoothness condition (its definition was also read); compact continuous norm bounds; measure-preserving coordinate extraction; and symmetric Fubini. Their normed-space, scalar, measure, countability and completeness premises are retained in their statements and applications. M004 was only a discovery probe, not a selected node. No external theorem is imported from Evans: that citation supplies the exercise identity in the frozen problem, not an extra proof premise, so no inaccessible primary theorem or deferred source is being assumed. The five producer units R001-R005 preserve all four original logical phases, including the explicit scalar equation calculation, domination/limit argument, coordinate FTC/Fubini calculation and final MVT constancy consequence; no material supplied calculation has been omitted. The graph's only roots are H and the nine selected M; every N and M lies in P's AND dependency closure and every N/P has exactly its displayed producer. The structural result is not mathematical acceptance; these are my same-author closing checks under the supplied shared criteria.\",\"readiness\":\"no_known_issue\",\"open_issues\":[],\"resolutions\":[],\"output_notes\":[{\"id\":\"N001\",\"note\":\"Checked /graph/propositions/@N001 and R001/S001-S003. The output exports both pointwise dot-product identities, not just their labels; R005 can invoke u_t·(u_tt−Δu)=0 without recalling R001's proof. The second-derivative identities and formula for every scalar satisfying the normality equation are established in S003 from differentiated constraint identities. All x,t,j ranges and the pointwise scalar condition are stated, and no smoothness of a is exported or used.\"},{\"id\":\"N002\",\"note\":\"Checked /graph/propositions/@N002 against R002/S001-S004. The output states the smoothness needed by later packets, the actual mixed-derivative identification and full formula for e_t, the t0-dependent slab, compatible existential C,R, Q and its measure, and the vanishing/integrability of every named scalar term. F001 and F002 supply the successive support/enclosing-radius choices; F003 and F004 supply derivative regularity and support; S004 proves integrability at every interior slab time and hence all positive times. This is adequate both for the guard of E and for the later joint compact bound, every-section FTC, and integral linearity uses.\"},{\"id\":\"N003\",\"note\":\"Checked /graph/propositions/@N003 against R003/S001-S003. The conclusion is differentiability of the actual finite function E at every positive time, together with the complete derivative-integral formula over ℝ^n. F002 gives a common integrable dominator and pointwise quotient limit, S003 applies the filter form of dominated convergence and identifies the integral quotient with the difference quotient of E. No mere formal differentiation or unstated limit exchange is exported.\"},{\"id\":\"N004\",\"note\":\"Checked /graph/propositions/@N004 against R004/S001-S003. Both integrands and their integrability, all positive times, and every spatial index are stated explicitly. F001 is the derivative-product identity; F002 proves the inner integral is zero for every remaining coordinate, not merely almost every one. The coordinate measure identification and symmetric Fubini give zero for ∫d, and linearity gives exactly the minus sign in the exported integration-by-parts formula.\"},{\"id\":\"P\",\"note\":\"Checked spec.conclusion and /graph/propositions/@P against R005/S001-S002. N002 supplies integrability and E's guard; N003 supplies differentiability and the derivative integral; N004 changes each spatial term; N001 cancels the pointwise normal acceleration. The displayed chain retains the factor two, finite sum and original normalization. S002 obtains constancy on the entire open positive-time interval, including equal endpoints in the local MVT estimate. The target is not weakened and there is no assertion at time zero.\"}],\"inference_notes\":[{\"id\":\"R001\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read the actual R001 packet (candidate 3, retained unchanged for candidate 4). S001 uses exactly H002 and H004 to differentiate the pointwise constraint using M006, and universally records tangency in F001. S002 uses only H005's pointwise scalar equation and F001 to get F002; it never differentiates the scalar. S003 differentiates the identities using H002,H004,M006 and the earlier F001, then dots the scalar equation with u and uses the finite definition of Δu. These are the actual roles of all four direct inputs; no compact-support, integrability or other original H is imported. Spatial and temporal identities are obtained on open domains and then evaluated at the fixed point. All quantifiers close and no additional local assumption remains.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M006/A001 at S001 uses K=ℝ,W=ℝ^m and f=g equal to the time section of u. H002 gives differentiability at t>0 and H004 makes its inner product constant. A002 at S003 uses u,u_t on time sections and u,u or u,u_j on spatial sections. Smoothness gives both differentiability premises in each instance; the dot-product derivative formula then has the exact terms displayed. Zero extensions of time sections are used only locally at positive times and change no derivative there. Norm squares equal real self-dot-products, so the factor two and signs follow by symmetry and finite algebra.\",\"declaration_check\":\"x,t are arbitrary for S001-S003 and correspond to the output quantifiers; j is arbitrary only for the S003 spatial calculation. The scalar a is a witness from the actual H005 at x,t and begins at S002; every use is within S002-S003. The last scalar computation explicitly depends only on its displayed equation, so applies to every satisfying scalar; its private identity does not escape. Functions and evaluation variables occurring only in source substitutions are bound within those substitutions. Global derivative symbols are supplied by D001-D004,D006, and no energy symbol or unsupported witness is used.\"},{\"id\":\"R002\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read the candidate-4 R002 packet. H001 is explicitly retained as the dimension clause in the output; H006 instantiated at t0/2,3t0/2 gives F001, and H002 gives smooth derivatives on the open domain. S001 obtains mixed symmetry with M007 and the density formula with M006. At S002 M008 on the compact witness C gives a norm bound; taking its maximum with zero plus one constructs an enclosing positive radius, including C empty. S003 uses the open complement of the closed compact C times int J, where u is actually constant, so successive derivatives vanish. It explicitly treats every scalar product and expands the last derivative by M006. S004 applies M005 only after F004 has proved continuity and compact support, and M008 gives the finite absolute-integral estimates. The same C works for the entire slab; no endpoint derivative at the time slab boundary is claimed. The basic finite-product compactness, Lebesgue box measure, local-constant derivative, and regularity closure steps are ordinary standard background with their conditions present; no project-specific result or missing core tool is hidden in them.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M006 at S001 differentiates the real inner products of time sections of u_t,u_j, with both differentiability premises from H002. M007 at S001 uses K=ℝ and the zero extension of u on ℝ^n×ℝ: H002 gives C² locally at every positive-time point and minSmoothness ℝ 2=2, so evaluation on coordinate vectors gives exactly ∂_t u_j=∂_{x_j}u_t=v_j. M008/A001 at S002 uses the identity map on the chosen compact C, hence yields the bound used to construct F002. M006/A003 at S003 uses the spatial sections of u_t and u_j, whose smoothness is already in F003. M005 at S004 uses ℝ-valued continuous sections on Euclidean Lebesgue space; F004 places the closure of every nonzero set in compact C. M008/A002 there uses these same continuous functions on compact Q. The measure is finite on compact sets, and each codomain has the required normed structures.\",\"declaration_check\":\"t0 is arbitrary and J is defined at S001. The compact witness C is not chosen before F001; it starts at S002. The radius R is not named as an available witness before F002; it starts at S003 with Q. Their scopes continue through S004, and the output existentially exports compatible witnesses dependent on t0, not a single set for all time. The expression-bound indices and points in F003,F004 have explicit ranges and binders; source-bound sample points remain bound in each application. The complete derivative, energy-density and Laplacian notation is in D001-D008; E is absent, so there is no circular use of its integrability guard.\"},{\"id\":\"R003\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read the candidate-4 R003 packet. Its only project input is the complete statement of N002, which directly supplies the common support witnesses, regularity, formula meaning and integrability at every positive time. S001 constructs η=t0/4 and I⊂(t0/2,3t0/2), then M008 proves F001. S002 uses the same box and time interval in the MVT estimate, divides only for |h|>0, and treats points outside Q separately; b is integrable because Q is measurable of finite measure and B is finite nonnegative. F002 records continuity/integrability of the quotients, the uniform bound and the pointwise limit. S003 uses M001 only with these earlier grounds. Integral linearity is applied to integrable densities and nonzero h. The quotient limit is the two-sided punctured derivative criterion at an interior positive time; no uncontrolled exchange or assumption of differentiability of E is used. Every direct input has its stated role.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M008 at S001 is used on Q×I with f=e_t extended outside the positive-time domain: this compact set lies strictly inside that domain, so its restriction is continuous by the derivative formula and smoothness in N002. The output bound is made nonnegative and selected only in the next S. M002 at S002 uses scalar real domain/codomain, convex I, the full scalar derivative converted to multiplication by e_t, and endpoints t0,t0+h in I; F001 supplies exactly its operator-norm bound. This yields |difference|≤B|h| before division. M001 at S003 uses Lebesgue ℝ^n, real-valued quotients F, and punctured neighborhoods of zero, with the displayed countable basis. F002 supplies eventual a.e. strong measurability via continuity, the stronger everywhere domination, integrable b and everywhere convergence. Its exact integral limit becomes E's derivative by the displayed linearity identity.\",\"declaration_check\":\"t0 is arbitrary; C and R are compatible witnesses from direct N002 at that t0. Q,η,I are explicit definitions from available data. B is a witness from the earlier F001, beginning only at S002. F is explicitly total by its piecewise definition, so values outside the valid quotient range do not evaluate u at forbidden times or divide by zero. b is defined from B and Q. Dummy x,r,h in functional definitions and quantified estimates are locally bound; no free sample point is exported. All objects remain scoped through S003, and N003 exports no private support or bound. D009 is used only with the direct guard N002.\"},{\"id\":\"R004\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read the candidate-4 R004 packet. Direct N002 provides the time-dependent support witnesses, n≥1, all smoothness, and integrability of d and both product terms. S001 uses M006 to obtain the actual product derivative and F001. Because C⊂int Q is closed, its complement is an open neighborhood of the box boundary, so all endpoint values vanish. S002 applies FTC separately to every fixed remaining coordinate; continuity on the closed interval proves interval integrability, rather than incorrectly inferring it from global integrability. The sections vanish outside [−R,R], so the full line integrals agree with the computed interval integral. S003 uses the coordinate measure equivalence and Fubini on an integrable function, not a formal iterated integral; F002 makes every inner integral zero. Integral linearity and symmetry give the exported minus sign. The n=1 case is explicitly the empty remaining-coordinate product of measure one. No original H or ancestor proof beyond direct N002 is used.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M006 at S001 has K=ℝ,W=ℝ^m, with the spatial sections of u_t and u_j smooth by N002. Its derivative terms are exactly v_j and u_jj. M003 at S002 has scalar f(z)=g(ι(z,y)), endpoints −R<R, differentiability on and beyond the closed interval from F001, and continuous derivative there; its output is the displayed endpoint difference, which is zero. M009 at S003 is used with k=n−1, coordinate spaces ℝ and index j−1; N002 gives n≥1 and the stated index range. Each coordinate volume is sigma-finite, so the extraction map identifies the domain measure with the indicated product. M010 uses the scalar function d∘ι on that product; F001's integrability transports through the measurable volume-preserving bijection, and both Lebesgue measures are s-finite. Its order of integration is precisely real z first and remaining y second, as required to invoke F002.\",\"declaration_check\":\"t0,j are arbitrary with the output's ranges. C,R are directly justified witnesses from N002 and Q is explicitly defined. g and d are explicit definitions from available derivatives, with their asserted smoothness proved from N002 in S001, not granted merely by their local types. The coordinate insertion ι is defined at S002 and its inverse extraction is the map supplied by M009; no unproved determinant or structural decomposition is assumed. y is arbitrary only in S002, then generalized in F002 using a fresh statement-bound y0. All later coordinate variables in integrals are expression-bound, and g,d,ι remain in scope through their last use at S003. The output contains only the global derivative fields and quantified time/index, not private witnesses.\"},{\"id\":\"R005\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read the candidate-4 R005 packet. S001 uses all four direct N inputs by their exported statements alone: N002 for integrability and the density derivative formula, N003 for the actual energy derivative, N004 for integration by parts at each finite spatial index, and N001 for pointwise cancellation. All linearly separated integrals are finite and the Laplacian substitution is the finite definition D006. The derivative computation is generalized to F001 before S002 uses it. S002 fixes arbitrary positive endpoint times, uses F001 and the MVT estimate on their closed interval, and concludes constancy including s=t. N002 remains a direct input for E's guard and the integrability clause. There are no additional original assumptions, limit arguments or undischarged conditional premises in this final inference.\",\"source_application_check\":\"The sole selected source here is M002 at S002. V=K=W=ℝ, f is the explicitly defined zero extension of E, S is the unordered closed interval with positive endpoints s,t, c=0 and L the zero linear map. F001 supplies derivative zero at every time in S; local agreement of the extension on positive times supplies the full derivative and therefore the within derivative. The zero norm bound, convexity and both endpoint memberships are all checked explicitly. The delivered estimate |E(t)−E(s)|≤0 gives equality. The earlier N inputs are used exactly in their global time/index ranges and require no appeal to their producer bodies.\",\"declaration_check\":\"The arbitrary t0 is scoped just to S001 and eliminated by the universal F001. The separate arbitrary positive s,t start at S002 and serve the constancy quantifier. The extension f is defined there from guarded E with direct N002 available; r in its piecewise formula is a function-bound variable, not a time-zero premise. Spatial x and indices j in the displayed integral/sum calculation are expression-bound. All global derivative and density symbols have D definitions and their index conventions agree with the N inputs. No local witness escapes and the original time domain remains (0,∞).\"}] }","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"defer_primary_source","description":"After actual unavailable primary-source access, preserve a complete exact secondary quotation as an explicitly unverified external assumption. The statement must match the quote in a supplied input. Returns the verification record for E.source.verification; this never grants ordinary Audit A PASS.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"source_id":{"type":"string"},"statement":{"type":"string"},"input_id":{"type":"string"},"quote":{"type":"string"},"attempts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["source_id","statement","input_id","quote","attempts"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report only a real substantive/suspected mathematical GAP, unavailable source or conflicting original input, with all five located fields. Ordinary unfinished NL0, source registration and JSON bookkeeping are not reports: continue an actual lookup or draft edit. TASK_INCOMPLETE is unavailable for NL0 authoring. Difficulty or a long run is not evidence of a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review. The optional module locator uses dotted syntax (Mathlib.Topology.Basic), never a slash path; omit it if unknown.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"find_library_sources","description":"Search pinned foundational metadata by an exact declaration name or ordinary mathematical terms. Ranked lexical candidates are not a theorem whitelist or an applicability judgment. Selected sources still need explicit M roots and complete checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible. For an existing string optionally supply both start_line/end_line to request up to 250 numbered lines and its complete text_sha256 for replace_lines. A read end beyond the text returns the remaining existing lines and actual range; the start must exist. Edits never clamp their range.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_author_packet","description":"Same-author closing inspection of one structurally valid own conditional inference: exact direct inputs, output, declarations and own proof. No ancestor bodies, extra H, independent reviewer or Audit A feedback.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"inference":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","inference"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_author_checks","description":"Save actual same-author notes and readiness against shared Audit A criteria. Unresolved/not-checked partial notes can be saved, but only complete actual packet inspection with no known issue can release a proof. Open issues persist until explicit located resolutions. No PASS or mathematical verdict is generated; independent Audit A receives none of these notes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"original_context_note":{"type":"string"},"readiness":{"type":"string","enum":["no_known_issue","unresolved","not_checked"]},"open_issues":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"criterion":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","criterion","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"resolutions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"output_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"inference_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"dependency_and_local_assumption_check":{"type":"string"},"source_application_check":{"type":"string"},"declaration_check":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","dependency_and_local_assumption_check","source_application_check","declaration_check"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["candidate","readiness","open_issues","original_context_note","output_notes","inference_notes"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"6cda3c1f-8ab9-4317-b846-e748acbc50d9","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"high"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":142162,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":45952,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4201,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":385},"total_tokens":146363,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d1b74508191ab91c4dbcbe22cdb":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":31,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d1e27088191b9f00f564f4783e1":{"input_tokens":30,"cached_tokens":30,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d2176f48191b750246b9d75d8dc":{"input_tokens":27,"cached_tokens":27,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d248d108191ae49163b9e74a704":{"input_tokens":37,"cached_tokens":37,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d282e808191bffea8d8f5ab5e55":{"input_tokens":37,"cached_tokens":37,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d2d673881918a8af32977b50427":{"input_tokens":38,"cached_tokens":38,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d331c808191b419feeedd1c0873":{"input_tokens":37,"cached_tokens":37,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d36c7b08191a516f96054368f73":{"input_tokens":27,"cached_tokens":27,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d3ea5b48191a4358ee806b6ea1b":{"input_tokens":66,"cached_tokens":66,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d4807a08191b97bc46c3576295f":{"input_tokens":36,"cached_tokens":36,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d909dd88191818752bfeae68630":{"input_tokens":35,"cached_tokens":35,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d94af288191a20fed4592465661":{"input_tokens":36,"cached_tokens":36,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0b9ca2ffc961a3af016ae49d98d99c8191880c65cb8072f174":{"input_tokens":37,"cached_tokens":37,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_token